RISC3D test kit 31 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 30 found the way round the Pi's Mesa bug: with lighting on, V3D
loses texture coordinates only while the texture matrix is the plain
identity. rol-3d 0.18 now keeps the texture matrix a hair away from the
identity (a change that does nothing to 2D textures), on V3D only.
Programs still see their own matrices; other drivers are untouched.

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 30.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.18-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/uploads memory
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
 3. Double-click Lit: all six parts should now show the checker.
 4. Run TORCS: the car should have its livery and cockpit, and the
    scenery its textures.

